WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.775
PostgreSQL has a precedence order for logical
operators NOT is evaluated

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.238
before AND and AND is evaluated before OR So A OR B

00:00:10.262 --> 00:00:13.162
AND C means A OR the combination of B AND C Knowing

00:00:13.188 --> 00:00:17.762
that rule is useful but relying on memory is risky
Parentheses make

00:00:17.788 --> 00:00:21.638
the intended business logic visible and protect the
rule when another person

00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:28.112
edits the query later For this course treat
parentheses as documentation When

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:31.688
AND and OR appear together group the related tests
explicitly so the

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:34.375
query is easier to explain and harder to misread
